# SunOS 4.1.1's miniroot copied from tape 1 into sd0b (M14 phase B;
# sim/mame/sunos.sh miniroot): the PROM boots MUNIX from the tape, MUNIX
# loads its own root into a RAM disk and asks what to do; the disk's label
# (sim/mame/mkdisk.py) is kept, and the miniroot goes to its b partition.
# sunos.sh runs this with PROMPT set to MUNIX's last question, which ends it.
\n> *@@b st()
Enter a 1 or 2: *@@1
Enter a 1, 2, or 3: *@@2
